From: Vitrine
Subject: [PATCH] usb-host: a device coming back has no address yet

usb_host_handle_reset() leaves alone a device that has no address yet, so
that the guest's reset while it enumerates a device is not a real one. But
only usb_device_reset() clears the address, after calling that handler, and
detaching does not: a device given by its IDs that is unplugged and comes
back still has the address of its last connection, and the guest's first
port reset goes to the host device, in libusb_reset_device(), with the BQL
held. The host has only just enumerated the device. If it does not answer at
once, the whole VM stands still for the 20 seconds and more of the kernel's
descriptor timeouts, and the kernel holds the device's lock for as long,
which stops any program reading the device's strings in sysfs.

Clear the address when opening the device, so that a reconnect goes as the
first connection does.
---
 hw/usb/host-libusb.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/usb/host-libusb.c b/hw/usb/host-libusb.c
index 629505c..c2cbc86 100644
--- a/hw/usb/host-libusb.c
+++ b/hw/usb/host-libusb.c
@@ -1049,6 +1049,13 @@ static int usb_host_open(USBHostDevice *s, libusb_device *dev, int hostfd)
                  "host:%d.%d", bus_num, addr);
     }
 
+    /*
+     * A device coming back is a new device: without this, the address of its
+     * last connection makes the guest's first reset a real one, see
+     * usb_host_handle_reset().
+     */
+    udev->addr = 0;
+
     usb_device_attach(udev, &local_err);
     if (local_err) {
         error_report_err(local_err);
